  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Please add a toggle to allow turning off any chromatic aberration post process effect. \n\nThere's already a 'Bloom Intensity' slider that allows users to interfere with whatever bloom setting world authors may have used, so I imagine it would be technically possible to introduce a toggle for chromatic aberration as well. \n\nI'm opposed to the use of chromatic aberration in VR. Headset manufacturers go to great lengths to minimize chromatic aberration in their optical systems only for misguided world authors to reintroduce it. It's especially ghastly to see when using a headset with pancake lenses.\n\nWorld authors often include post processing toggles but without any fine-grained control. In these cases, a toggle for chromatic aberration in VRChat's menu would allow removal of chromatic aberration without sacrificing the artist's other presentation choices like color grading, tonemapping, bloom, etc.\n\nPerhaps the toggle could be called \"Allow Chromatic Aberration\" and it could sit in the \"Accessibility -> Display and Visual Adjustments\" section.",
